    "message": "feat(fallback): rate-based eject + retry-once + bench-off toggle\n\n- settings.py: FALLBACK_EJECT_WINDOW / _FAILURE_RATE / _MIN_SAMPLES\n  (rate-based eject knobs), FALLBACK_BEHAVIOR (rate_based/legacy),\n  FALLBACK_RETRY_FIRST (skip/retry_once), FALLBACK_BENCH_ENABLED\n  (bool, default false = old direct-retry/direct-fallback behavior).\n- route_health.py: RouteHealthRegistry gains bench_enabled (default\n  True for registry instances; Settings default makes it False via\n  the factory). When False, every method no-ops. When True, kind-aware\n  bench durations: 5xx/transient -> 1s, rate_limit -> provider\n  Retry-After, auth/permission/quota -> eject_seconds, sustained\n  rate-based -> eject_seconds.\n- execution.py: route_health_registry(settings) threads\n  bench_enabled into the registry cache key.\n- admin/manifest.py: register FALLBACK_BENCH_ENABLED as a select\n  (false/true, default false) in the limits section.\n- tests: _ejection_settings accepts bench_enabled (default True);\n  FALLBACK_BENCH_ENABLED added to the LIMIT_KEYS contract tuple.\n\nBench OFF is the default on new installs. Opt in per-route via the\nadmin page or FALLBACK_BENCH_ENABLED=true in .env.",
